# Naming Rules

## Default: camelCase everywhere
Variables, functions, non-exported constants, folders, and non-component files use `camelCase`.

```typescript
// ✅ Correct
const userName = "Ali";
const maxRetries = 3;
function fetchUserData() {}

// ❌ Forbidden — snake_case / kebab-case
const user_name = "Ali";
const max-retries = 3;
```

## Exceptions (the only allowed deviations)
```typescript
// ✅ Exported constants and enum values — UPPER_SNAKE_CASE
export const MAX_RETRIES = 3;
export const API_BASE_URL = "/api";
enum Status { ACTIVE, NOT_FOUND }

// ✅ Types, interfaces, enums, React components — PascalCase
interface UserProfile {}
type FilterOptions = {};
enum UserRole {}
export const UserCard = () => <div />;
```

## Boolean and handler prefixes are required
```typescript
// ✅ Required
const isLoading = true;
const hasError = false;
const canEdit = true;
const handleSubmit = () => {};
const handleClick = () => {};

// ❌ Forbidden — no is/has/can or handle prefix
const loading = true;
const onSubmit = () => {}; // use handleSubmit inside the file, expose as onSubmit only via props
```

## File naming by type
| File type | Convention | Example |
|-----------|------------|---------|
| React component | `PascalCase.tsx` | `UserCard.tsx` |
| Hook / model | `camelCase` with `use` prefix | `useUserModel.ts` |
| Store | `camelCase` with `Store` suffix | `userStore.ts` |
| API | `camelCase` with `Api` suffix | `userApi.ts` |
| Types file | always `index.ts` | `types/index.ts` |
| Everything else | `camelCase` | `formatDate.ts` |

## Forbidden
```typescript
// ❌ PascalCase folders
widgets/UserProfile/

// ❌ snake_case anywhere (except UPPER_SNAKE_CASE constants)
const user_id = 1;

// ❌ kebab-case variables/folders
const user-id = 1;
widgets/user-profile/

// ❌ Props interface without Props suffix
interface UserCard {} // should be UserCardProps
```
